  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 155 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nSunday through Friday:\n\nSteady as she goes in the extended period as there haven't been\nmany forecast changes from the previous days. High pressure is\nexpected to dominate the weather pattern through at least\nWednesday, with dry conditions and light to moderate southerly\nwinds starting Monday after light and variable winds on Sunday.\nThere will be a warming trend as a ridge develops over the \ncentral Plains Sunday morning and translates east over the\nMidwest Monday through Wednesday. Highs in the upper 40s on\nSunday should steadily increase through the week, with highs\naround 60 possible on Friday.\n\nRain may finally return on Thursday as both the GFS and ECMWF\ndepict low pressure moving over Western Ontario, dragging a cold\nfront over the Midwest. How much rain/rain coverage remain in\nquestion however, as right now both global models show a strong\nhigh over the southeastern US blocking appreciable moisture flow\nfrom the Gulf. PoPs remain in the 15 to 30% range at this time.\n\nCMiller",
